    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260-a2">

                <pb facs="1037" n="887" xml:id="pg887"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gummeré to Mr. George C. Reed.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-03-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Reed</hi>: I have received your letter of
                    February 20 last, informing me of your continued difficulties in securing a
                    proper house at Mequinez, notwithstanding the Sultan’s orders to the basha of
                    that place, as well as the vizier’s assurances to myself. I am more annoyed than
                    I can say as to this and have written and dispatched a strong letter to the
                    vizier demanding an explanation, in the name of my Government, of this breach of
                    his solemn engagement with me and insisting on the immediate fulfillment of the
                    same. I will also communicate with the Department of State on the subject. I
                    will inform you at once as to the result of my representations to the vizier,
                    Ben Sliman.</p>
                <p>With kind regards and best wishes for a favorable solution of the matter of your
                    house, believe me,</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. R. Gummeré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
